# Astro/Node.js build artifacts. site/dist/ and site/.astro/ were tracked
# (207 files) despite this rule — committed before it existed, and tracked
# files ignore .gitignore. That broke the deploy strip: `npm run build` is not
# byte-reproducible (the embedded search index reorders), the entrypoint builds
# on every boot, and deploy.py treats any changed tracked file outside
# ALLOWED_PREFIXES as `unexpected`, which sets DeployPreview.blocked. Netlify
# builds from source (netlify.toml: base = "site", command = "npm run build"),
# so nothing needed them committed. Untracked 2026-09-08, Gate 12.
dist/
.astro/
.build/
.output/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Cache directories
.cache/
.tmp/

# Environment variables
.env
.env.local
.env.*
!.env.example

# Admin-only SQLite state (Gate 12, 2026-09-08).
# These two are their own source of truth, never rebuilt from published
# content, and claims.db holds requester PII — names, email addresses,
# submitted patches and Stripe customer ids. Four separate code comments
# already asserted they were gitignored; until now nothing here said so, and
# the only thing keeping them out of a public repo was deploy.py's
# tracked-file guard, which guards the deploy path and not a manual `git add`.
# data/directory.db and data/factchecks/ stay tracked — they are derived,
# committed artefacts.
data/claims.db
data/articles.db
data/outreach.db
data/backups/
data/audit.log

# Working directories the deploy guard already refuses to publish from
# (deploy.py GUARD_PATHSPECS) — named here too so they can never be staged
# in the first place.
temp_data/
content-staging/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Logs
*.log

# Editor/IDE files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
